# WordPress PHP style

- Tabs, not spaces. Use `array()`, not `[]`.
- Spaces inside parens: `if ( ! $foo )`, `__( 'Text', 'maintenance-tools-wcus26' )`.
- Yoda: `if ( 'post' === $type )`. Wrap long lines (~110 chars) before `&&`, `||`, `.`.
- Empty methods on two lines. Do not use `function foo() {}`.

```php
protected function before_run(): void {
}
```

# PHPDoc

- Short summary ending with a period, then `@since 1.0.0`.
- `@param` / `@return` include a description, not only a type. Add `@global wpdb $wpdb` when using `$wpdb`.
- Hooks: “Filters …” / “Fires …”. Overrides of parent methods may use `{@inheritdoc}`.
- Class docblocks describe purpose; do not write `Class Foo`.
